pman @alpha 0.6

pman (short for postman) is a formatted delivery tool. Like a mailman, it
does exactly three things:

    * Parse mails into a structured format
    * Decide whether a mail is deliverable based on user groups and
      delivery permissions (not implemented yet)
    * Report the processing result through main()'s return value

The database it produces can be rendered into a static site by webb
(web builder, my other project).

If you want to dig deeper into the code, read main(). I believe good code
explains itself.
